Dear Dr Landis,

Your manuscript, "Consumption Based Responsibility for Global Warming and t=
he Distribution of Impacts of SwissClimate Policy", has now been assessed.

I have now received two reports on your paper by two very good referees. Th=
e reports of the referees are just great. There is a lot in them. I agree w=
ith the referees and I am therefore offering to you the opportunity of revi=
sing the paper.=20

You should follow very closely their requests and in particular you should =
focus on fleshing out the statistical analysis of the determinants of the G=
HG footprints (if possible). I also agree with the suggestion of referee 1 =
to simulate more sophisticated climate policies. One additional suggestion =
is to use a simple index (such as, for example, the Suits index as in Ander=
sson, Julius J., and Giles Atkinson. The Distributional Effects of a Carbon=
 Tax on Gasoline: The Role of Income Inequality) to compare the degree of r=
egressivity of the different climate policies you simulate.=20

If you decide to go ahead with the revision, needless to say, please submit=
 the short text describing the main changes made and also the point-by-poin=
t replies to all the feedback together with the revision. Good luck!

If you need more time, please contact us and include your submission ID.

Kind regards,

J=C3=A9r=C3=A9my Laurent-Lucchetti
Editor
Swiss Journal of Economics and Statistics=0A=
